    "created_at": "2026-02-12T08:08:10Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-02-12T08:08:10Z",
    "body": "In current versions of Chrome and Firefox ESR, `:disabled` matches `<option>` nested in `<optgroup>` nested in `<select>` nested in `<fieldset>` when either `<select>` or `<fieldset>` has the `fieldset` attribute specified. It does not match when only `<optgroup>` has the `disabled` attribute specified.\n\nThis is not compatible with the current definition of this algorithm in all cases.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Example</summary>\n<br>\n\n```html\n<style>\n  option:disabled {\n    outline: 2px solid red;\n  }\n</style>\n<form>\n\n  <fieldset disabled>\n    <select>\n      <optgroup>\n        <option></option> <!-- red outline -->\n      </optgroup>\n    </select>\n  </fieldset>\n\n  <fieldset>\n    <select disabled>\n      <optgroup>\n        <option></option> <!-- red outline -->\n      </optgroup>\n    </select>\n  </fieldset>\n\n  <fieldset>\n    <select>\n      <optgroup disabled>\n        <option></option> <!-- no red outline -->\n      </optgroup>\n    </select>\n  </fieldset>\n\n  <fieldset disabled>\n    <select>\n      <optgroup disabled>\n        <option></option> <!-- red outline -->\n      </optgroup>\n    </select>\n  </fieldset>\n  \n</form>\n```\n\n</details>\n\nShould this algorithm find `<datalist>` or `<form>` before it can return anything?\n\nWPT has a [test](https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/blob/c12c26e12df02a81af21545b625f658c971c3e20/html/semantics/selectors/pseudo-classes/disabled.html#L23-L26) that all browsers pass and that expect `:disabled` to match `<option disabled>` nested in `<optgroup disabled>` nested in `<select disabled>`. There should be 3 separate test cases defining the `disabled` option on only one of them imo.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
