    "created_at": "2026-02-13T04:20:43Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-02-13T04:20:43Z",
    "body": "  > Thanks for the example.\n\nPlease disregard it and (most of) my preceding comment. Chrome and Firefox are conforming to the current algorithm. (They make `<option>` become disabled when they are inside a disabled `<optgroup>`.)\n\nI think I actually used `:is(select, option):disabled` instead of `:disabled` in the test. `<option>` does not render an outline, so the visible outline should have told me that the test was incorrect. Sorry. \n\nThis confusion aside, I still think it would make sense to make `<option>` disabled when it is in a disabled `<select>` or `<fieldset>`, except there is a `<datalist>` between `<select>` and `<option>`.",
